#
# The clause of incomparable_membership_clause.guard written twice, in two rules, byte for byte. Each
# draws the incomparable-membership notice over the incomparable-membership templates, and the two
# notices open with the same words (the clause as written) and differ only in the position each ends
# with. Over the pair of templates both are drawn by the second file too, so the trailer after the run
# has two plain notices of one kind to tell apart.
#
rule incomparable_membership_first {
    Name not IN [10, 50, 100]
}

rule incomparable_membership_second {
    Name not IN [10, 50, 100]
}
